## 1. Add The OpenNext Adapter To Each App

The files live in `references/cloudflare/` next to this file. For each web app:

1. Copy `open-next.config.ts` into the app folder.
{% if "web-user-app" in app_ids %}2. Copy `wrangler.web-user-app.jsonc` to `web-user-app/wrangler.jsonc` and `dev.vars.web-user-app.example` to `web-user-app/.dev.vars.example`.
{% endif %}{% if "web-admin-portal" in app_ids %}2. Copy `wrangler.web-admin-portal.jsonc` to `web-admin-portal/wrangler.jsonc` and `dev.vars.web-admin-portal.example` to `web-admin-portal/.dev.vars.example`.
{% endif %}3. Add the dependencies and scripts to the app's `package.json`:

```json
{
  "scripts": {
    "build:cloudflare": "npm run clean && opennextjs-cloudflare build",
    "preview": "npm run build:cloudflare && opennextjs-cloudflare preview",
    "deploy": "npm run build:cloudflare && opennextjs-cloudflare deploy"
  },
  "devDependencies": {
    "@opennextjs/cloudflare": "1.15.1",
    "esbuild": "0.27.3",
    "wrangler": "4.77.0"
  }
}
```

The `clean` script must also remove `.open-next`: `"clean": "node -e \"const fs=require('fs');['.next','.open-next'].forEach(d=>{try{fs.rmSync(d,{recursive:true,force:true})}catch(e){}})\""`.

4. Keep the `__name` definitions in the app's `next.config.mjs` (the `webpack` hook that defines `__name` and `__name__`); the Worker bundle needs them.
5. Add the build output and the local secrets file to `.gitignore` for each app:

```gitignore
{% if "web-user-app" in app_ids %}web-user-app/.open-next/
web-user-app/.wrangler/
{% endif %}{% if "web-admin-portal" in app_ids %}web-admin-portal/.open-next/
web-admin-portal/.wrangler/
{% endif %}.dev.vars*
!.dev.vars.example
```

## 2. Configure Non-Secret Worker Variables

Edit each app's `wrangler.jsonc` before the first deploy.

{%- if "web-user-app" in app_ids %}

### `web-user-app/wrangler.jsonc`

Set these values to your deployed backend URL and public web URL:

| Variable | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `API_BASE_URL` | Server-side calls from NextAuth and route handlers |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL` | Browser-visible API base URL |
| `AUTH_URL` | Public URL of the deployed user web app |
| `AUTH_TRUST_HOST` | Keep as `true` behind Cloudflare |
{% if "google" in auth_methods %}| `AUTH_GOOGLE_ID` | Google OAuth client ID |
{% endif %}{% if "apple" in auth_methods %}| `AUTH_APPLE_ID` | Apple service/client ID |
{% endif %}{% if "facebook" in auth_methods %}| `AUTH_FACEBOOK_ID` | Facebook app ID |
{% endif %}{% if "microsoft" in auth_methods %}| `AUTH_MICROSOFT_ID` | Microsoft client ID |
| `AUTH_MICROSOFT_TENANT_ID` | Microsoft tenant ID, often `common` |
{%- endif %}
{%- endif %}

{%- if "web-admin-portal" in app_ids %}

### `web-admin-portal/wrangler.jsonc`

Set these values to your deployed backend URL and public admin URL:

| Variable | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `API_BASE_URL` | Server-side calls from NextAuth and route handlers |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL` | Browser-visible API base URL |
| `AUTH_URL` | Public URL of the deployed admin portal |
| `AUTH_TRUST_HOST` | Keep as `true` behind Cloudflare |
{%- endif %}

