## 6. Backend Interop

If your backend is deployed to Azure Container Apps (see `azure-setup.md`), set `CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` there to match the public Cloudflare URLs for the web apps. Otherwise the browser apps can deploy successfully but fail CORS checks against the backend.

## Optional: GitHub Actions Deploy

The generated CI lints, type-checks and builds only. To deploy on every push to `main`, add a deploy job to the app's workflow such as the one below (shown for `web-user-app`; change the folder and the name for another app). It reports **Deploy skipped** and does nothing while a secret is missing. Before deploying, the validation job can also run `npm run build:cloudflare` and `npx wrangler deploy --dry-run` to check the Worker bundle.

```yaml
  deploy:
    name: Deploy to Cloudflare
    needs: lint-typecheck-build
    if: github.event_name == 'push' && github.ref == 'refs/heads/main'
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    environment: production
    env:
      PRISM_RELEASE_CONFIGURED: {% raw %}${{ secrets.CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN != '' && secrets.CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID != '' }}{% endraw %}
    steps:
      - name: Report skipped deploy
        if: env.PRISM_RELEASE_CONFIGURED != 'true'
        run: |
          echo "::warning title=Deploy skipped::Set the CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN and CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID secrets to deploy the web app. No deploy ran."

      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
        if: env.PRISM_RELEASE_CONFIGURED == 'true'

      - name: Set up Node.js
        if: env.PRISM_RELEASE_CONFIGURED == 'true'
        uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with:
          node-version: "22"

      - name: Install dependencies
        if: env.PRISM_RELEASE_CONFIGURED == 'true'
        working-directory: web-user-app
        run: npm install

      - name: Deploy worker
        if: env.PRISM_RELEASE_CONFIGURED == 'true'
        working-directory: web-user-app
        run: npm run deploy
        env:
          CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN: {% raw %}${{ secrets.CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN }}{% endraw %}
          CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID: {% raw %}${{ secrets.CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID }}{% endraw %}
```

### Required GitHub Secrets

| Secret | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID` | Cloudflare account ID |
| `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` | API token with Workers edit permissions |

